msgid "Mathlib Benchmark"
msgstr "Mathlib-maatstaf"

#: src/mathlib.c:960
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s=%s states the thread count of every library that honors it, so a thread "
"benchmark measures the same count on every pass.  Unset it and restart to "
"benchmark thread counts."
msgstr ""
"%s=%s stel die draadtelling van elke biblioteek wat dit eerbiedig; 'n "
"draadmaatstaf meet dus dieselfde telling met elke deurgang. Ontstel dit en "
"herbegin om draadtellings te meet."

#: src/mathlib.c:970
msgid "Benchmarks are disabled while optimization is activated."
msgstr "Maatstawwe is gedeaktiveer terwyl optimalisering aktief is."

#: src/mathlib.c:977
msgid "You must load a NEC2 input file before running benchmarks."
msgstr "Jy moet 'n NEC2-invoerlêer laai voordat maatstawwe uitgevoer word."

#: src/mathlib.c:983
msgid ""
"Choosing a benchmark other than \"Single Job\" has no effect unless -j is "
"specified on the command line."
msgstr ""
"Die keuse van 'n maatstaf anders as \"Enkele Taak\" het geen effek tensy -j "
"op die opdragreël gespesifiseer word nie."

#: src/mathlib.c:1000
msgid "You must select at least one math library to benchmark"
msgstr "Jy moet ten minste een wiskundebiblioteek kies om te toets"

#: src/mathlib.c:1005
msgid "Run the benchmark now?"
msgstr "Is jy seker jy wil die maatstaf nou uitvoer?"

#: src/mathlib.c:1006
#, c-format
msgid ""
"This will run a frequency loop benchmark for each detected linear algebra "
"library and then provide a summary.  It may take some time to complete "
"depending on how big and how many frequencies your NEC2 will use. Detailed "
"timing will be provided in the terminal.\n"
"\n"
"Notes:\n"
"* Only one Intel MKL library can be tested without restarting xnec2c, so "
"select which one you wish to benchmark before proceeding or it will choose "
"the first in the list and skip the rest.\n"
"\n"
"* Thread congestion will occur for multi-threaded libraries when using the -"
"j N option if there are not enough CPUs available to accommodate the forked "
"processes in combination with library threads.  Consider reducing the value "
"of -j N for benchmarking to find what library works best with a mix of "
"forking and threading; you can use `top` to monitor your CPU usageand if it "
"reaches 0%% idle then you might consider reducing -j N.\n"
"\n"
"Consider experimenting with the --threads N option, which states the thread "
"count of each job in place of the equal share of the processors it receives "
"otherwise.  An exported thread-count variable states that count itself and "
"overrides both, and --threads is refused while one is set.\n"
"\n"
"This dialog will close when the benchmark completes."
msgstr ""
"Dit sal 'n frekwensielusmaatstaf vir elke bespeurde lineêre-"
"algebrabiblioteek uitvoer en dan 'n opsomming verskaf. Dit kan tyd neem om "
"te voltooi, afhangend van hoe groot en hoeveel frekwensies jou NEC2 sal "
"gebruik. Gedetailleerde tydsberekening sal in die terminaal verskaf word.\n"
"\n"
"Aantekeninge:\n"
"* Slegs een Intel MKL-biblioteek kan getoets word sonder om xnec2c te "
"herbegin; kies dus die een wat jy wil meet voordat jy voortgaan, anders kies "
"dit die eerste in die lys en slaan die res oor.\n"
"\n"
"* Draadophoping sal vir multigedrade biblioteke voorkom wanneer die -j N-"
"opsie gebruik word indien daar nie genoeg SVE's beskikbaar is om die "
"geforkte prosesse saam met biblioteekdrade te akkommodeer nie. Oorweeg om "
"die waarde van -j N vir maatstawwe te verminder om te vind watter biblioteek "
"die beste met 'n mengsel van fork en drade werk; jy kan `top` gebruik om jou "
"SVE-gebruik te monitor en as dit 0%% ledig bereik, kan jy oorweeg om -j N te "
"verminder.\n"
"\n"
"Oorweeg om met die --threads N-opsie te eksperimenteer, wat die draadtelling "
"van elke taak stel in plaas van die gelyke deel van die verwerkers wat dit "
"andersins ontvang. 'n Uitgevoerde draadtellingveranderlike stel daardie "
"telling self en oorskryf albei, en --threads word geweier terwyl een gestel "
"is.\n"
"\n"
"Hierdie dialoog sal sluit wanneer die maatstaf voltooi is."

